{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_15-25-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && grep -n \\\"core_overview\\\\|behavior\\\\|Behavior\\\\|Fact\\\\|map_path\\\\|graph_path\\\" audit-method.md | head -60\"","aggregated_output":"7:You own reading, investigation and construction; the controller owns source/version relationships, accepted products, formal execution and attribution. Activity → Behavior → Fact → Candidate → Obligation → Evidence expresses dependencies, not required turns. Partial maps and sourced unmapped Surfaces are valid; formal Candidates need an accepted map basis. Follow the analysis guide for selection and handoff, the review guide for evidence, and the task contract for submission. Respect authorization, budgets and independent fresh runs throughout.\n13:Follow guide.md using the controller's activity_roles. No preset protocol API or historical bug is required. Behavior/fact analysis and tool choice serve the selected discriminator.\n19:First explain both core relationships from activity_roles and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Follow representative work through owners, qualified support, aggregation, decision, propagation and consumption; explain acquisition, change and loss of context/authority and handling of old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions. Read the supporting membership, history, recovery and completion mechanisms needed for this backbone. Trace callers and callees, important rejection, retry and asynchronous paths; deeper variants may remain open.\n21:Save early discrepancies as sourced Surfaces or specific unknowns even when no obligation is ready. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: unexplained formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks readiness; a usable overview can retain local anomalies. Only a preconfigured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary first; activity_focus does not. A usable map and first Candidate may share a product. Unmapped source work and exploration need no fabricated Fact.\n23:Use behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n27:When sourced mechanisms answer the specific suspicion, submit explained and reselect. An unconstructed single obligation may remain unexecuted; this is neither holds nor a budget refund. Fixed artifacts, directed execution tasks, changed premises and open disputes remain visible until explicitly handled. An explicit guard with unresolved ownership, timing, producer or context instead calls for investigation of that premise. A negative result should identify the plausible explanation it excluded and independent premises left open; distinguish it from execution corroborating an already-explained protection. Neither settles the entire Fact or becomes a reason to expand input variants indefinitely. Keep one requirement's independent scenarios together; a genuinely different responsibility gets its own question.\n33:At natural handoffs retain the answered proposition and remaining discriminator in feedback using tasks/audit.md references. In the next already-needed related map submission, replace the answered original unknown with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete progress reminders. Correct materially misleading higher-level summaries in that same product before reuse; harmless wording differences need no cleanup turn or whole-map sweep. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment, not an understanding label or reference alone. Use behavior-facts.md for primary ownership instead of copying one answer across layers. Source work and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning.\n41:Initial understanding covers consensus formation/advancement and context/authority transitions together. Explain their actual connection: which support remains eligible across which transition, who can consume it, and how pending work or prior decisions constrain subsequent formation. Per-instance ownership is a valid context; no global leader, term, log or fixed majority is assumed. One later Candidate may focus on only one core line. Keep necessary supporting behavior at its actual coordinate and explain cross_activity_effects rather than relabeling it.\n49:Shared updates do not imply shared follow-up effects. When one entry establishes a fact and schedules a consumer but another only establishes the fact, preserve that distinction in trigger, important_branches, writes, external_effects or async_boundaries. Do not union effects into an unconditional guarantee. Distinguish possible effects, conditional scheduling and guaranteed completion. A Behavior can cover multiple entries when conditions remain clear; split minimally when owners, completion boundaries or meanings cannot be expressed accurately together. Do not enumerate every branch or duplicate a shared Fact.\n51:Fact states the assertion actually established for its identity and validity_context, not the strongest effect seen on any path. Reporting, internal accounting, notification and completed external work are distinct. Trace relevant guard inputs to their producer, update point, owner and completion duty instead of trusting a variable name. Conversely, a missing local field is not a missing guarantee when dispatch, admission, serialization or reset supplies it. Assess the composed producer/consumer protection, not each structure in isolation. Absent direct action is a question: inspect alternative consumers, delayed validation, shared scheduling and recovery for the same object and history before alleging a defect.\n57:Keep one primary home for each kind of knowledge: Behavior owns producer conditions, changes, synchronization, notification and exit mechanisms; Fact owns the assertion for its identity and validity_context; Candidate/feedback owns the question's answer, actual execution and remaining discriminator; Activity/core_overview owns the core connections, higher-level understanding and navigation; Surface owns unread entries and reasons; CheckRun/assessment/review owns experiment progress and judgments. Scope owns exclusions. Preserve substantive overviews without copying the same long answer and residuals through every layer. Mapped means association, not resolution. An explained Candidate needs no challenge merely to restate its protection; changed protection or Fact context does require attribution. Use the guide's natural handoff for answered unknowns and tasks/audit.md for Material and execution references.\n76:EXECUTION Observe actual implementation effects under explicit inputs, caller policy and authorized isolation. Contract applicability may remain unresolved during exploration; execution permission may not. A changed value or tests_passed is not a violation oracle. Exploration remains construction knowledge: a later requirement needs a separately fixed check, fresh execution and correspondence review, not retroactive relabelling. Missing capability, compilation failure, timeout, panic and a completed property comparison remain distinct. Retain failures; never precompute expected observations or alter protocol behavior to create a finding.\n78:COMPLETION Separate the proposition's observation endpoint, necessary caller completion, and resource cleanup. A normal nonzero test exit may leave a completed violating witness intact only through checker_correspondence.execution_attribution binding the exact target CheckRun, checker and valid event indices, retained failure stream lines and fixed harness lines. Use source_ids and rationale to justify that all duties needed by that witness completed before an independent failure, with no corruption of history, identity or values. Machine validation checks these references and eligibility, not causal independence; stdout/stderr line numbers are not a common clock. Ordinary no_issue_found never authorizes nonzero exits. Preserve raw failure, other scenario debts and later challenges; no holds-only, timeout, cancellation, signal, build failure, missing premise, ambiguous or contradictory observation can use this path. Do not remove required join/close, ignore exceptions or kill workers after printing to manufacture PASS; unsupported short wall-clock limits are not extra properties. Changed harnesses, premises, predicates or scope still need the existing new-artifact and actual-execution path. Initialization, driver compliance and observation validity belong in prerequisites, controls or diagnostics, not duplicate properties. Check a wait's return or record actual attainment when it establishes a necessary premise; when waiting is the investigated behavior, requiring success would discard the failure history. Sleep establishes elapsed time, not synchronization, completion or a coherent snapshot; a printed readiness flag is not a prerequisite witness. A diagnostic control need not satisfy the principal scenario's premises or acquire a separate obligation: select formal applicability from independently declared input/policy fields before execution, retaining control output. Distinct formal scenarios need their actual admission and premises; incompatible histories may need separate checks. Never select scenarios by observed results or missing premises after execution. Role readiness does not imply that earlier work drained. Across preparation, policy changes and delivery, preserve caller/transport duties; prefer one policy-selected delivery path and record the identity, provenance and order needed for attribution. Distinguish receipt, per-message-type queueing and dispatch; preserve the replaced layer's ordering without assuming global FIFO or arbitrary reordering. Legal in-flight work need not be emptied. End controlled work independently of the forbidden behavior. Observe admission, completion and final state for the same operation before treating absence as bounded holds. Missing completion, identity, result events and tool timeout remain unknown. A finite window records non-completion, not a deadline violation or infinite stalling. A repeatable suffix must account for behavior-determining state, schedule, queues, timers and callbacks; equal business fields do not close execution. A rescue stimulus may itself be required caller work.\n82:MEANING Distinguish the written obligation, the proposition encoded by applicability/trigger/antecedent/assertion, and what this execution actually compared. Type, count or numeric-position equality may be necessary without establishing content or identity equality. Record comparisons and scope limits separately. Identify live object, copy, cache or caller-maintained observations, their writers and the synchronization or ownership boundary supporting the read; multiple fields must represent the state the proposition needs. Include ownership of injection flags, counters and sampling itself. An export discrepancy need not mean active protocol state changed. Match observation to the claim: stopping may change the behavior; neither shutdown sampling, locks, public APIs, dual reads nor race detection are universally required. Challenge specific unreliable reads, not all concurrent checks. Keep unresolved contracts, counterevidence, input legality and observation differences explicit; CheckRun owns execution status. An implementation/requirement discrepancy is the subject, not a conflict between requirement sources. Real contradictions remain conflicts.\n93:Write a complete submission.json using submission.schema.json and product-schemas.json. Cite authorized captured ranges. Follow next_objective and the analysis guide for core_overview readiness; a usable map and first Candidate may share a submission.\n99:- research: submit substantive feedback alone with acquired source or retained execution ref_ids, or a complete partial map_path, additive graph_path or scope_path. Feedback alone needs no Candidate or usable overview and creates no map version or Evidence. An identical adjacent pure handoff on unchanged research receives duplicate_of: accepted without new knowledge; continue useful investigation, not rewording. A map may accompany one graph/scope operation. semantic_revision supplies an attributed F2/F3 feedback_path for an existing unit_id and may carry a map. Graph additions cannot invent unowned executable Units.\n108:A formal question names one principal fact_ids entry, lifecycle, direct behavior_ids, sourced A1/A2 relationship, contexts, event_paths, importance and trigger_rationale. supporting_behavior_ids maps distinct Behavior IDs to their causal role. audit_spec_version may be omitted for the current basis. A map file's version is its accepted base (1 initially); the controller assigns resulting versions, including questions in combined products and F2/F3 patches. Do not guess current+1. Unchanged Candidates retain their historical basis. A supporting-layer question cites its actual consumer or core relationship and declares the supported A1/A2 activity; a local storage obligation need not become a whole-cluster consequence. If that relationship lacks sources, investigate or retain feedback instead of inventing a core label.\n110:The controller derives actual map differences and reverse indexes. map_changes explains modified/removed objects and new producers or consumers of an existing principal Fact, with impact (clarification/meaning/dependency), acquired source_ids and rationale. Use one preserves explanation for unchanged requirements, dependencies and observation scope, or challenges mapping saved Candidate IDs to specific disputed premises. A corrected principal Fact requires a challenge; clarification cannot disguise identity/context/edge changes or removal. Independent additions need no invented revision and may still challenge a prior interpretation.\n114:For every feedback shape, including one accompanying a map, Candidate or review, ref_ids directly includes each saved CheckRun whose execution it explains, alongside relevant Candidate, Behavior, Fact, surface:<entry_point> and Material IDs. Obtain execution IDs from research.json.explorations[*].executions[*].check_id or the exact records locator, not operation/plan IDs or prose. Explaining only a repaired execution references only that run; a joint explanation references both failure and repair and distinguishes their observations. Shared sources, Behavior or harness names do not associate executions. Source-only answers need no execution reference. Map/map_changes source_ids remain Material references. understanding records learning, not a map change; use the guide's natural handoff. question_updates revises Candidate unknowns/resume_conditions with sources, retaining requirements and counterevidence. Historical remaining is then-remaining; current execution/review records remain authoritative.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
